air/OS (Haiku arm64): Mesa 26.2.4's PowerVR Vulkan driver on the native
"powervr" kernel driver (/dev/graphics/powervr/0, Cubie A7S BXM-4-64 MC1).

The kernel takes Linux's drm.h / pvr_drm.h structures unchanged behind op
codes PVR_HAIKU_OP(nr) (headers/private/graphics/powervr/pvr_haiku.h in the
air/OS tree, put on the include path by build.sh, not copied). All changes are
#ifdef __HAIKU__ or Haiku-only meson except two in pvr_physical_device.c, a
NULL check and an assert fix; a Linux build of this tree is otherwise
unchanged (build.sh builds the host tools and the drm-shim smoke test from
it).

  include/drm-uapi/drm.h            BSD ioctl encoding from <bsd/sys/ioccom.h>
  include/drm-uapi/pvr_drm.h        no <linux/const.h>, <linux/types.h>: _BITULL
  include/xf86drm.h                 libdrm stand-in (Haiku only, #include_next
                                    elsewhere): drmIoctl() -> ioctl(fd,
                                    PVR_HAIKU_OP(req & 0xff), arg,
                                    IOCPARM_LEN(req)), retried on EINTR/EAGAIN;
                                    drmGetVersion/FreeVersion/GetCap/DropMaster;
                                    drmSyncobj* (create, destroy, wait, reset,
                                    signal, timeline signal/wait, query,
                                    transfer) as libdrm, but -1 + errno on
                                    failure and ETIME for every timeout; PRIME
                                    and syncobj/sync-file fds fail with
                                    EOPNOTSUPP until pvr_haiku.h names their
                                    ops; drmDevice types, an empty
                                    drmGetDevices2(); static asserts that the
                                    op numbers and sizes match pvr_haiku.h
  src/util/u_sync_provider_haiku.c  the Vulkan runtime's syncobj provider on
  src/util/u_sync_provider.h          those wrappers, timelines when the kernel
  src/util/meson.build                answers DRM_CAP_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE
  src/vulkan/runtime/meson.build    build vk_drm_syncobj.c without libdrm
  src/vulkan/runtime/vk_image.[ch]  keep drm_format_mod (pvr_image.c and
                                    EXT_image_drm_format_modifier use it)
  pvr_instance.c                    no device list: open HAIKU_PVR_DEVICE or
                                    /dev/graphics/powervr/0, accept it if
                                    DRM_IOCTL_VERSION says "powervr", describe
                                    it as a platform device with a render node
                                    only; driver build hash from the version and
                                    the loaded library file's size and mtime
                                    (dladdr + stat; the version alone if that
                                    fails): no build-id note at run time
  pvr_physical_device.c             VK_EXT_physical_device_drm: render 0:0, no
                                    primary node (stat() of a NULL path is
                                    skipped); and an upstream bug (also in
                                    main): without the shader cache,
                                    pvr_physical_device_free_pipeline_cache()
                                    asserted disk_cache != NULL and so aborted
                                    every vkDestroyInstance in a build with
                                    assertions (debugoptimized)
  pvr_arch_job_transfer.c           pvr_queue_transfer()'s submission
                                    (some 380 KiB: the prepare array) on the
                                    heap, not the submitting thread's stack
                                    (256 KiB by default on Haiku)
  winsys/powervr/pvr_drm_bo.c       CPU maps through PVR_HAIKU_NR_MAP_BO (a
                                    clone of the buffer's area; placed maps
                                    free the reservation and pass the address),
                                    unmapped with delete_area(); "reserve"
                                    unmaps leave a PROT_NONE mapping

Not changed: the heap size (util/os_misc.c: sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES), which
Haiku's libroot answers from get_system_info()); the conformance gate
(PVR_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER=1); bxm-4-64.h (26.2.4's is identical to
Mesa main's, gs_rta_support off and usc_alu_roundingmode_rne on); mutexes
(every mutex in src/imagination is initialized explicitly).

